row", "meaning_zh": "\u19999 \u12289 \u25291 " \} ] \}, "mnemonic": \{ "root_memory": "COM\u65288 \u19968 \u36215 \u65289 + JACERE\u65288 \u19999 \u65289 \u8594  \u25226 \u27794 \u26377 \u26681 \u25818 \u30340 \u24819 \u27861 \u32113 \u32113 \u19999 \u21040 \u19968 \u22602 \u21435 \u29468  \u8594  \u30606 \u29468 ", "story_en": "Without clear data, the scientists could only THROW (jacere) random theories COM- (together) as mere CONJECTURE.", "story_zh": "\u22312 \u27794 \u26377 \u26126 \u30906 \u25976 \u25818 \u30340 \u24773 \u27841 \u19979 \u65292 \u31185 \u23416 \u23478 \u20497 \u21482 \u33021 \u25226 \u38568 \u27231 \u30340 \u29702 \u35542 \u19999 \u65288 JACERE\u65289 \u22312 \u19968 \u36215 \u65288 COM\u65289 \u65292 \u20316 \u28858 \u19968 \u31278 \u32020 \u31929 \u30340 \u12300 \u25512 \u28204 \u65288 CONJECTURE\u65289 \u12301 \u12290 ", "emojis": ["\u10067 ", "\u55356 \u57266 ", "\u55358 \u56809 "] \}, "example": "The media's reporting on the celebrity's disappearance was based entirely on conjecture rather than hard facts.", "example_zh": "\u23186 \u39636 \u23565 \u36889 \u20301 \u21517 \u20154 \u22833 \u36452 \u30340 \u22577 \u23566 \u23436 \u20840 \u26159 \u22522 \u26044 \u25512 \u28204 \u65292 \u32780 \u38750 \u30495 \u24977 \u23526 \u25818 \u12290 ", "collocations": [ "pure conjecture", "matter of conjecture", "scientific conjecture", "open to conjecture", "fuel conjecture" ], "synonyms": ["speculation", "guesswork", "surmise", "hypothesis"], "near_synonyms": [ \{ "word": "speculation", "difference": "speculation involves constructing broad, complex commercial or philosophical theories based on loose evidence; conjecture is a specific, single guess made on the spot due to missing pieces." \}, \{ "word": "hypothesis", "difference": "hypothesis is a formal, structured scientific proposition designed to be tested through systematic experiments." \} ], "antonyms": ["fact", "certainty", "proof", "reality"], "word_family": [ \{ "word": "conjecture", "pos": "noun / verb" \}, \{ "word": "conjectural", "pos": "adjective" \} ], "frequency_rank": 93, "frequency_source": "custom", "difficulty": "C1", "tags": ["college", "GRE", "academic"] \}, \{ "word": "conspicuous", "pos": "adjective", "phonetic": "/k\u601 n\u712 sp\u618 kju\u601 s/", "definition": "Standing out so as to be clearly visible; attracting notice or attention.", "definition_zh": "\u39023 \u30524 \u30340 \u65307 \u24341 \u20154 \u27880 \u30446 \u30340 \u65307 \u26126 \u39023 \u30340 ", "etymology": \{ "roots": [ \{ "root": "com-", "origin": "Latin", "meaning": "intensive prefix", "meaning_zh": "\u21152 \u24375 \u35486 \u27683 " \}, \{ "root": "specere", "origin": "Latin", "meaning": "to look", "meaning_zh": "\u30475 " \} ] \}, "mnemonic": \{ "root_memory": "COM\u65288 \u23436 \u20840 \u65289 + SPECERE\u65288 \u30475 \u65289 \u8594  \u35731 \u20154 \u32085 \u23565 \u26371 \u30475 \u35211 \u30340  \u8594  \u26997 \u28858 \u39023 \u30524 \u30340 ", "story_en": "Her bright neon jacket made her highly CONSPICUOUS, forcing everyone to LOOK (specere) straight at her.", "story_zh": "\u22905 \u37027 \u20214 \u26126 \u20142 \u30340 \u38675 \u34425 \u22846 \u20811 \u35731 \u22905 \u39023 \u24471 \u38750 \u24120 \u12300 \u24341 \u20154 \u27880 \u30446 \u65288 CONSPICUOUS\u65289 \u12301 \u65292 \u36843 \u20351 \u27599 \u20491 \u20154 \u37117 \u30447 \u33879 \u22905 \u30475 \u65288 SPECERE\u65289 \u12290 ", "emojis": ["\u55358 \u56762 ", "\u55358 \u56730 ", "\u55357 \u56385 \u65039 "] \}, "example": "The red warning sign was placed in a conspicuous position near the high-voltage entrance.", "example_zh": "\u32005 \u33394 \u35686 \u21578 \u27161 \u35468 \u34987 \u25918 \u32622 \u22312 \u39640 \u22739 \u38651 \u20837 \u21475 \u38468 \u36817 \u19968 \u20491 \u39023 \u30524 \u30340 \u20301 \u32622 \u12290 ", "collocations": [ "conspicuous consumption", "highly conspicuous", "conspicuous position", "conspicuous lack of", "conspicuous success" ], "synonyms": ["noticeable", "prominen